From: TunaOS Package Factory <packages@tunaos.org>
Subject: [PATCH] session: pass the resolved normal session name before opening

A normal session can use its saved or fallback name without an explicit
SelectSession request. Open initiates saving the worker's account settings,
so send the already-resolved name before Open rather than only when the
session menu is used. Keep program-session settings and session selection
precedence unchanged.

Source: GDM 51.1.1 (d643e68963ab74564955025b554ec23cd794770d)
---
 daemon/gdm-session.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

--- a/daemon/gdm-session.c
+++ b/daemon/gdm-session.c
@@ -2995,6 +2995,13 @@ gdm_session_open_session (GdmSession *self,
                 send_display_mode (self, conversation);
                 send_session_type (self, conversation);
 
+                if (!self->is_program_session) {
+                        gdm_dbus_worker_call_set_session_name (conversation->worker_proxy,
+                                                               get_session_name (self),
+                                                               conversation->worker_cancellable,
+                                                               NULL, NULL);
+                }
+
                 gdm_dbus_worker_call_open (conversation->worker_proxy,
                                            conversation->worker_cancellable,
                                            (GAsyncReadyCallback) on_opened, conversation);
